nswer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186237558}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "4c5a6195-b8ed-52d4-86b4-4695109267db" :question/math-academy-id "q-103279" :question/problem "If $cos⁡x=\\frac{3}{8},$ then $4cos⁡(x-10\\pi )+5=$" :question/worked-solution "The period of $y=cos⁡x$ is $2\\pi .$ Therefore, for an integer $n$ we have\n\n$$\ncos⁡x=cos⁡(x+2n\\pi ).\n$$\n\nSubstituting $n=-5$ into the right-hand-side of the above gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}cos⁡x=cos⁡(x+2\\cdot (-5)\\cdot \\pi )=cos⁡(x-10\\pi ).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, if $cos⁡x=\\frac{3}{8},$ then $cos⁡(x-10\\pi )=\\frac{3}{8}.$\n\nFinally, then\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4cos⁡(x-10\\pi )+5 & =4\\left(\\frac{3}{8}\\right)+5 \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{2}+5 \\\\  & =\\frac{13}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186338802 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a0e7978b-65fb-572d-9e69-fb0ed478e885" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337487} {:answer/id #uuid "c8d773d6-1137-500e-9144-d700b2fde742" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}-10\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337808} {:answer/id #uuid "d9c26a46-9433-52e8-869e-79e45ee386aa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}-2\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337927} {:answer/id #uuid "de73e983-b2d8-5bee-8dbc-77304e29d367" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337970} {:answer/id #uuid "e38b4e0e-34f4-5b2c-bf38-151d565a04ef" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{2}+10\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338018}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a0e7978b-65fb-572d-9e69-fb0ed478e885" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337487} :answer-field/id #uuid "dd7d23c2-12b8-516e-b527-7ded32873395" :answer-field/key "sele