n/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "6abcc021-8010-5554-b152-291688c68aef" :question/math-academy-id "q-70672" :question/problem "If $cos⁡x=\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}$ for some $x$, then $cos⁡(x+16\\pi )=$" :question/worked-solution "The period of $y=cos⁡x$ is $2\\pi .$ Therefore, for any integer $n$ we have\n\n$$\ncos⁡x=cos⁡(x+2n\\pi ).\n$$\n\nSubstituting $n=8$ into the right-hand-side gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}cos⁡x=cos⁡(x+16\\pi ).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, if $cos⁡x=\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3},$ then $cos⁡(x+16\\pi )=\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186511918 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "13fa977c-7ab9-5f02-9a0c-1946b173eb62" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{12}{7}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186511917} {:answer/id #uuid "43c63a3e-8c7e-5f9c-bed5-8356fb6459df" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{30}{7}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186511927} {:answer/id #uuid "5f9f5765-9e63-51b4-81f2-ac00398068a2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{16}{7}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186511935} {:answer/id #uuid "715877e7-423a-52e2-ba4f-128b52c9eff6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{15}{7}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186511942} {:answer/id #uuid "bb8b713e-6030-54a2-bb0e-99ba1fba2a32" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{12}{7}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186511965}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5f9f5765-9e63-51b4-81f2-ac00398068a2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{16}{7}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186511935} :answer-field/id #uuid "88b4427d-f2f1-571e-900c-ab2a00e3a774" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186511951}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "19ee0877-fb33-5fe0-9855-c6ff1fa21c11" :question/problem "If $\\cos x=\\frac{1}{7},$ then $2\\cos (x-14\\pi )+2=$" :question/worked-solution "The period of $y=\\cos x$ is $2\\pi .$ Therefore, for an integer $n$ we have\n\n$$\n\\cos x=\\cos (x+2n\\pi ).\n$$\n\nSubstituting $n=-7$ into the right-hand-side of the above gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\cos x=\\cos (x+2\\cdot (-7)\\cdot \\pi )=\\cos (x-14\\pi ).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, if $\\cos x=\\frac{1}{7},$ then $\\cos (x-14\\pi )=\\frac{1}{7}.$\n\nFinally, then\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2\\cos (x-14\\pi )+2 & =2\\left(\\frac{1}{7}\\right)+2 \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{7}+2 \\\\  & =\\frac{16}{7}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186511924 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5f260668-83d5-5737-be7a-fcd41740577c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{19}{7}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186511934} {:answer/id #uuid "7534c7ed-b9b9-5a4e-b7cc-648e83cbe230" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{34}{7}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186511943} {:answer/id #uuid "7b4eb6cc-0bc2-52a2-b07f-504b6d6ecb53" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{6}{7}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186511945} {:answer/id #uuid "c55cc9ed-9a42-5e6f-9fff-988edf9b714f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{34}{7}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186511967} {:answer/id #uuid "e8d21f26-67b9-5b1e-b9e7-725f74bfd9d4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{76}{7}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186511976}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7b4eb6cc-0bc2-52a2-b07f-504b6d6ecb53" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{6}{7}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186511945} :answer-field/id #uuid "e5a37119-64a0-594b-a7bb-6f870c3ecc3e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186511975}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "24687af9-7fd4-5bfe-b0b9-67927f085480" :question/problem "If $\\cos x=\\frac{5}{7},$ then $-4\\cos (x+10\\pi )+2=$" :question/worked-solution "The period of $y=\\cos x$ is $2\\pi .$ Therefore, for an integer $n$ we have\n\n$$\n\\cos x=\\cos (x+2n\\pi ).\n$$\n\nSubstituting $n=5$ into the right-hand-side of the above gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\cos x=\\cos (x+2\\cdot 5\\cdot \\pi )=\\cos (x+10\\pi ).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, if $\\cos x=\\frac{5}{7},$ then $\\cos (x+10\\pi )=\\frac{5}{7}.$\n\nFinally, then\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-4\\cos (x+10\\pi )+2 & =-4\\left(\\frac{5}{7}\\right)+2 \\\\  & =-\\frac{20}{7}+2 \\\\  & =-\\frac{6}{7}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186511954 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2d6da1e2-0fc0-5147-801e-aeba9fd0a4e3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186511925} {:answer/id #uuid "65e48e25-48e0-5afc-a62f-b9d4d703c71f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2} + 2 \\pi" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186511938} {:answer/id #uuid "66a734e0-d488-5c53-a570-c5e45521b909" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186511939} {:answer/id #uuid "7c302d7c-4ebb-5d84-a744-489a4c514931" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2 \\pi -\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186511947} {:answer/id #uuid "efcddf52-2dfc-505f-9694-44c61e1244af" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2} + 2 \\pi" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186511978}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "66a734e0-d488-5c53-a570-c5e45521b909" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186511939} :answer-field/id #uuid "1d38747a-6c0f-5e3e-987a-1170bec732be" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186511920}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/i